519","description":"Christiaan Huygens","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7901-ab39-8a503bd25822","description":"Johannes Kepler","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-720b-afac-774194f246be","description":"Galileo Galilei","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7330-b9e5-6fa1d7e19bbe","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which of the following conditions can lead to blindness if left untreated?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A cataract clouds the eye\u2019s lens; surgery can restore sight by replacing the cloudy lens with an artificial one.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7eac-bb99-6dc66490d31b","description":"Cataract","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-71d0-8ecf-8abfcd0f753d","description":"Arthritis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-72c0-9363-7c9609e431a1","description":"Mumps","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7f8a-bb89-d768c6d4103b","description":"Jaundice","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-797c-86da-84ff17ebfcd0","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What determines the color of our skin?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Melanin absorbs ultraviolet radiation, helping protect skin cells from sun damage; differences in its amount and type contribute to skin color.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-77fc-bbec-17327ea68bd5","description":"Melanin","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7fb5-9f06-40b818ddec15","description":"Collagen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-77a6-8161-035980177809","description":"Cadmium","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-79d2-8a75-9841bef6377d","description":"Calcitonin","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-752c-a8bf-ba33db7ab400","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which lizard is able to change the color of its skin?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Chameleons often change color to signal mood or regulate body temperature, not just to blend into thei