ence that studies the origin, history, and structure of the Earth?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Geologists use rocks, fossils, and landforms to reconstruct how the planet has changed over time.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7a00-9c58-6ec034afb3ad","description":"Geology","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7173-8c19-6f18566e6b72","description":"Astronomy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-75db-a7be-81f1ebd3f96d","description":"Magnetism","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-750e-97c5-bb33b04cbd7a","description":"Meteorology","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-73d3-bc3e-eb916c41e826","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name for a great wave resulting from an earthquake?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Tsunamis are caused by large-scale water displacement, often from undersea earthquakes, rather than by ordinary tides.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7210-86e7-94e69794424c","description":"Tsunami","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7a43-b1df-5cb812a7a8d6","description":"Kahuna","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7b37-9e3e-0375d948b62b","description":"Overflow","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7f58-ba51-3ee8c84eceab","description":"Grand Masif","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7b58-a77d-0d23b65a5ce8","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"On which continent do no bees live?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Antarctica has no native bee populations; its harsh climate and limited flowering plants cannot support them.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7672-be8b-af7159ea2836","description":"Antarctica","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7bd6-956f-78ba445f30fa","description":"Australia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7d3b-9716-75fc45335cf2","description":"Asia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-744e-a4e8-be28170eae2d","description":"Africa","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-