"Cabbage","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7960-8a2e-ce2c907f4600","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which of the following is not a planet?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The Moon is Earth\'s natural satellite, orbiting Earth rather than the Sun directly.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-722a-acdb-a1506e9ccb5f","description":"The Moon","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-76c2-ab5b-dc13dae8563f","description":"Mars","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-792d-9195-b1402bc24452","description":"Jupiter","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7a8a-942a-264af568eec5","description":"Mercury","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-72cb-a9e9-5c9576c2e605","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What does the word \"chlorophyll\" mean in its Greek origin?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Chlorophyll absorbs light for photosynthesis; its Greek name combines chloros, meaning \u201cgreen,\u201d and phyllon, meaning \u201cleaf.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7e74-84b7-3310d1292e20","description":"Green leaf","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-712a-961a-bf2091d66292","description":"Brown bark","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-734e-b1a6-a98246759603","description":"Red flower","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7518-96ab-5c1f8c1bfe09","description":"Juicy fruit","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7471-b25e-19fddd532a44","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"When chopping an onion, which glands in the eyes produce tears?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Onion vapors irritate the eyes and trigger reflex tear production by the lachrymal glands.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-73aa-bac8-0690fa060b55","description":"The lachrymal glands","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-79f9-9d37-598b268d7551","description":"The salivary glands","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-780b-b23d-716b083c4f67","