"correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-73dd-b475-f6c0ebadb169","description":"Earth","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-724a-aa88-8d0180999bd9","description":"Uranus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7ae5-8207-a13d777f2812","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the process by which both milk and blood can become semisolid?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Clotting occurs as fibrin forms a mesh in blood; in milk, proteins gather into curds, as in cheese-making.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7ef9-8e21-356f3a964a48","description":"Clotting","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-719b-b75d-1c9da5eb89e7","description":"Pasteurization","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7255-99b4-cd22808e0aef","description":"Filtration","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-78eb-bf09-d338838a1f38","description":"Distillation","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7d72-ab91-6071f0abd2d2","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the term for a mineral that contains metal?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"An ore contains enough valuable material to make extraction worthwhile; not every metal-bearing rock qualifies.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7984-b91f-7afaa2ce477b","description":"Ore","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-75a1-b04d-52a7c05577c8","description":"Peat","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7aa5-9465-10d98a1edb36","description":"Stone","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7791-a77d-e9c5589edf8c","description":"Cement","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7fd4-8c08-ba28f5fb282f","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"A female deer is known as what?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A doe is also an adult female rabbit; an adult male deer is called a buck.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7ff7-89bd-34e7fe2f6064","description":"A Doe","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7f86-9da3-2c46328f40c4","description":"A Pen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7030-bb4b-cdf69032e862","description":"A Mare","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-76fd-b67b-b61523d3f2a5","description":"A Nanny","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-798b-a2e8-b3b4e93438bb","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What kind of organism is a leech?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A leech is a parasite because it feeds on a host; many species use suckers to attach to animals.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7bdf-a80e-aac7676150e5","description":"Parasite","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-70c1-acb1-0ac81ad74c56","description":"Herbivore","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7a79-9f5f-d3203c9a7631","description":"Omnivore","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7c8a-9bbe-3bdb20cff9a1","description":"Decomposer","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7630-a299-c32772dce6a8","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the largest snake?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Anacondas are generally considered the largest snakes by weight, though reticulated pythons can grow longer.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7468-8e45-cf07103de7cf","description":"Anaconda","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-764c-95a4-bb0f0783e115","description":"Black mamba","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7739-a005-163be650b0bb","description":"Rattlesnake","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-716b-867b-907716ec4c59","description":"King cobra","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-73de-9b5c-82edfeb548e9","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What type of shape might be obtuse or isosceles?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A triangle\'s angles total 180 degrees; obtuse describes one angle greater than 90 degrees, while isosceles means two sides are equal.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7b7d-8df6-74f5e80c30b6","description":"A Triangle","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-74b6-8e95-5ede63cdea9d","description":"A Square","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7368-8d80-0c0d6d589462","description":"A Circle","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7012-9ae1-ea4a3e4ebe69","description":"A Rectangle","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7581-b8c7-e561a0067b4a","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is made out of gravel, sand, cement and water?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Concrete hardens as cement reacts with water, binding the sand and gravel together.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-74d7-82c6-78adc1a2bcbe","description":"Concrete","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7dfe-bf6b-00789d9179dc","description":"Porcelain","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7162-83a0-73f935a78cf1","description":"Gypsum","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-758a-b352-568bfd190b45","description":"Chalk","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-700c-b505-343a0cebb540","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"How many limbs does an octopus have?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"An octopus has 8 limbs, usually called arms. They contain no bones, which helps the animal squeeze through narrow spaces.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7daf-9b0c-d60335b6c66b","description":"8","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7f5e-8c86-431a2fb2cde1","description":"6","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-76e6-bd79-5a756e1d3e19","description":"10","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7435-84bd-c1c14ce73987","description":"14","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4e-7b04-b723-81acde5e0a6b","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"The chemistry of life centers around which element?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Carbon has four valence electrons, allowing it to form stable bonds with many elements and build the chains and rings found in biomolecules.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-a