ca. Despite the name, it is the largest dolphin species.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7ae9-91cb-6c645d99da39","description":"Killer whale","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7341-80c5-b81b83e9741d","description":"Badger","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-70da-8876-e8dda46bef61","description":"Orchard bee","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7681-972a-4bf8124be9a4","description":"Camel","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7abf-90ed-2fd9d76502cc","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which bird often stands on one leg?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Flamingos filter tiny organisms from water and mud with their distinctive bills, which they hold upside down while feeding.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7b12-9b00-c58627d03c0f","description":"Flamingo","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7f30-bfb3-a3b49f0cb3d9","description":"Hummingbird","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7421-a657-1adaedd9e800","description":"Ostrich","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7ae4-86ef-c1ccdcd6cd05","description":"Pigeon","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7d53-8da7-c4de8724426d","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the unit of linear measurement?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The meter is defined using the speed of light in a vacuum: light travels one meter in 1\/299,792,458 of a second.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7fd5-acec-1ffeba5b953b","description":"Meter","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-78d5-8ce5-a4d5a352192f","description":"Decibel","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-74e8-b5ac-ffafd2a63a73","description":"Coulomb","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-721c-a44f-09e9a0eba5b3","description":"Ampere","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7f17-9d31-e8a3caf71e96","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"For what does the fourth letter in \"NASA\" stand?","difficulty":1,"e