},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7b44-9ad9-17bd0aa82645","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What force keeps the water in the oceans?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Gravity holds ocean water to Earth, while the Moon\'s gravity also helps create tides.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-73d0-a7f2-7dc529e50364","description":"Gravity","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7acc-8ded-25e9becb9403","description":"Friction","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7b65-8d2a-15b579894ecd","description":"Magnetic force","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7f21-9923-f91694f4302a","description":"Air resistance","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-713d-b5ff-26d9744feb94","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What was created with the big bang?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The Big Bang was the expansion of the early Universe, not an explosion into preexisting empty space.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-76e1-b2d3-073a1a5c1a6a","description":"The Universe","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7d91-a1ed-d389cfb607b9","description":"The Milky Way","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7f3d-b024-42a0fbe2e816","description":"Andromeda","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-743b-af7d-483ba4c7508e","description":"Infinity","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7220-8fa7-bb925ad8ea4f","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"A female horse is known as what?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A mare is an adult female horse; a young female horse is called a filly.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7384-bcf5-ff9d0f470f8e","description":"A Mare","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-77a3-84bc-19ca0fb1d118","description":"A Hen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-755d-8cbe-51d32a82ed2c","description":"A Hembra","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7ecc-93ac-2ccb80af037d","description":"A Jill","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-