":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7b50-92f0-0487e5effe1b","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Pediatrics is the branch of medicine that provides care for which of these groups?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Infants receive pediatric care, and pediatricians also treat patients through adolescence.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7545-82af-85253c5b4a18","description":"Infants","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7612-adf1-638e3be23d76","description":"Elders","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7e58-8128-18bca161946e","description":"Veterans","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7dda-ba10-01ca558c83a2","description":"Women","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7a4d-8c9d-e64d24a32a27","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the death of an entire species?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Extinction is global when no individuals of a species remain anywhere; disappearing from one region alone does not count.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7875-aa4f-4a504c4af256","description":"Extinction","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7f5d-b67b-e92ee4bd7732","description":"Adaptation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7daf-b9d4-081676d02470","description":"Evolution","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7447-9976-3c83c3ef32a7","description":"Migration","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-77d8-ac22-daf26a39aaa1","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What does pH measure?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A pH of 7 is neutral; lower readings indicate greater acidity, while higher readings indicate greater alkalinity.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7809-af9b-e036cbca9b5e","description":"Acidity and alkalinity","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-77b5-a8ee-85b6e0524166","description":"Temperature","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7fee-8940-6ee73d60f88b","description":"Density","correct_answer":false},{