","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7bb9-89c6-1256fd91fc09","description":"nutrition","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7c79-8d26-9aee77431824","description":"the signification and application of words","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7cde-bb03-753d5b0ea1c3","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What acts as an exchange surface between mother and embryo?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The placenta attaches to the uterine wall, and the umbilical cord carries substances between it and the fetus; their blood supplies generally remain separate.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7abe-810a-d19e37a405e1","description":"Placenta","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7d96-bcad-25170ec3539a","description":"Ovaries","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-788a-acc9-37aeae61fa6f","description":"Cervix","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-79ed-9a0c-7b8cbc6ffa60","description":"Anus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7725-9de6-be0e08bc3c92","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What cell component is often used for personal identification?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"DNA carries inherited genetic information, and forensic profiling compares variable regions to help distinguish people.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7c96-a4e8-0a09a4c65bbd","description":"DNA","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7271-8f4b-b6d5fa7648da","description":"Golgi","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7697-8f75-1e253aa70ddb","description":"Membrane","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7c14-b7aa-5f76e1eb83d4","description":"Cytoplasm","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7310-ae49-0227c09c06fe","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is a decrease in hemoglobin or the number of red blood cells?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Anemia can cause weakness and shortness of breath because less oxygen reaches the body\'s ti