 Current Diode","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7b03-ba35-8f0b0049a4be","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the square root of 144?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A square root is a number that, multiplied by itself, gives the original value; 12 \u00d7 12 = 144.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-70bd-ad3b-a67a56c59f34","description":"12","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7f2e-b967-3ac338b689ad","description":"11","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7b00-976d-33b81e3bf09e","description":"13","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7042-927b-f6cb27dba736","description":"14","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-73a2-92fe-abe5517ba27b","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What instrument is made by rubbing a needle with a lodestone and floating it on a piece of wood in water?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A compass works because its magnetized needle aligns roughly north\u2013south with Earth\'s magnetic field.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7390-8e54-c6d0f92858fe","description":"Compass","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-713c-9ae5-80ab5b9f0a3f","description":"Dynamo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7c1a-bddb-8127cfa3139e","description":"Geiger counter","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7345-b5d2-818653948da9","description":"Chronometer","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7fdb-b548-1da1da753275","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What silk structure do many insects use as a protective covering of the pupa?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A cocoon is a silk casing spun by many larvae; a chrysalis is the pupa itself, not its covering.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7435-a85e-8b8352073f34","description":"Cocoon","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-72ff-ae78-039af7b96de1","description":"Chrysalis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-791c-ac50-3575ab83fe90","desc