4","description":"Stork","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-77c6-a018-264a5f1cff4e","description":"Eagle","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-722f-b22a-31b66b74e981","description":"Swan","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-760e-9f1d-459885fcdf8b","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Who is considered the inventor of the first commercially practical light bulb?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Thomas Edison developed a durable incandescent lamp and a practical electric-lighting system, helping make electric lighting commercially viable.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-740c-b79a-a5e1a8611efe","description":"Thomas Edison","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7f99-8f94-25c5ecacc489","description":"Rudolf Diesel","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7833-9001-26e358dad9fa","description":"John Fowler","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7a0e-93a7-6b50e7b25243","description":"Johannes Gutenberg","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7484-8d27-5845faeaabd6","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"How many leaves does a shamrock have?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Three is the traditional leaf count; a four-leaf clover is a rare variation often treated as lucky.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7c8c-a232-eb90da76de21","description":"3","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-70f2-9de3-3439fb76423c","description":"2","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7484-9b9d-7c482609dcd2","description":"4","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7fc3-9c88-001aa781e980","description":"5","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7578-a9bf-09612c0c4546","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is a doctor who specializes in the care of infants, children and teenagers called?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Pediatricians care for children\'s health broadly, while oncologists specialize in cancer treatment.","alternatives":[{"