cstudy.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7829-8fb5-15e3e28a791d","description":"Life","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-78f3-be61-adad62826fdf","description":"Bell ringing","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7468-b4ac-2f8fc7a2232d","description":"Rheumatic diseases","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-70fa-8f2f-64e715ee774d","description":"Syphilis","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-75a6-b450-191b134e341a","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which scientist is said to have been inspired to develop his theory of gravity by a falling apple?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Isaac Newton\'s law of universal gravitation describes the same force pulling an apple toward Earth and keeping planets in orbit.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7bed-ba0e-b71c257bf9a7","description":"Isaac Newton","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7f8c-a2d9-c7fd0d5e90aa","description":"Charles Darwin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7b67-9b7f-5df54bf75162","description":"Galileo Galilei","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7595-aeed-bb196828153e","description":"Ernest Rutherford","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7948-a811-a863584c662a","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a female fox?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A vixen is a female fox; a male fox is often called a dog, and a young fox is a cub.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7d51-9c07-e2f57f866930","description":"A Vixen","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-702e-920a-5e4499ef1e52","description":"A Ewe","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7612-b522-1e4cca67679e","description":"A Hen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-71c7-914a-7c59784bf41c","description":"A Doe","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-72fe-9aef-a1b1617538b7","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Siamese and Burmese are breeds of which animal?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Cats of the Siamese breed commonly have blue eyes and color-point coats, while Burmese cats typically have short, glossy coats.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7b5e-8671-08b5a9ab65b0","description":"Cat","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-70b4-b4e6-9bea6bbdb2fd","description":"Dog","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7b60-a8b3-3b1944a6c4ab","description":"Donkey","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-79ea-a46c-9f8902c4ac86","description":"Pig","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7d45-97e0-d0f716b96aea","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Who is known for his theory of evolution by natural selection?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Charles Darwin presented his theory in On the Origin of Species, drawing on observations from his voyage aboard HMS Beagle.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7bd0-8d82-9b3d4c9e7897","description":"Charles Darwin","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-79b7-912a-733e6ebdfc84","description":"Albert Einstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7bbf-b624-478339807ef6","description":"Niels Bohr","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7590-a9e0-64a8b258e1cc","description":"Sigmund Freud","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7765-836b-c5c9e788a1b5","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"How many karats are in pure gold?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"24-karat gold is considered pure; lower ratings indicate that other metals make up part of the alloy.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-79e7-be96-f74d5942c9e1","description":"24 karat","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7f5a-b95c-60f20a8b323a","description":"22 karat","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-70fd-b4c9-bf582b387ac2","description":"30 karat","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7118-a757-0acb8b328ee8","description":"12 karat","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7a59-a887-4d80bb0cf6e8","category"