":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-755e-89f1-5afe5628f42a","description":"Standard model","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7c4b-a370-5ae5083bb728","description":"Special relativity","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7ee8-b8c2-af1031ced49b","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the direct cause of Type I Diabetes?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"In Type I diabetes, the immune system destroys insulin-producing beta cells in the pancreas, so blood glucose can build up.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7777-b476-ecc980810d42","description":"Not enough insulin","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-748e-bdb4-ab489a706a0e","description":"Not enough estrogen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7056-b504-9b999a9348de","description":"Not enough calcium","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-74aa-af21-3a81cca92ea5","description":"Not enough magnesium","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-70d0-b46f-870df28cdb2a","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the transition from liquid to solid phase?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Freezing is the reverse of melting; boiling and condensation are phase changes involving a gas.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-71f8-96f2-b6e67bad1828","description":"Freezing","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7f47-b26b-87bff83775c9","description":"Melting","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7887-ae9f-501da9eb0492","description":"Boiling","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-78b3-8d2a-792ba72ce791","description":"Condensation","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-72f4-abd3-ffcf7ac30fef","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name given to the practice of growing plants in liquids rather than soil?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Hydroponics supplies plant roots with nutrients through a water-based solution. The name combines Greek roots meaning \u201cwater\u201d 