dcc8","question":"In the human body, what is the name of the structure that runs down the middle of the back?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The spinal cord is part of the central nervous system, along with the brain.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-752b-8649-39fa473b663b","description":"Spinal cord","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7d30-9ad8-30c378536c4d","description":"Vagus nerve","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7cd5-88ea-986d154fac03","description":"Ribcage","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7599-8086-facffebd92ec","description":"Trachea","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7037-aaae-38cbf4fb8d4d","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What part of an exhaust converts toxic byproducts of combustion into less toxic ones?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A catalytic converter uses precious metals to transform carbon monoxide, nitrogen oxides, and unburned hydrocarbons into less harmful gases.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-787d-9a5d-a1cab19f68dc","description":"Catalytic Converter","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7a3a-9910-d8bd7c0453a2","description":"Muffler","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-718b-ba7f-eea337fb8062","description":"Exhaust Manifold","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7525-adec-ae832499a721","description":"Turbocharger","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7f8d-bbb4-6583d3ea87e1","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"A power station with turbines on tall towers on hills or at sea generates electricity from which energy source?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Wind turbines turn wind\'s kinetic energy into electricity; \'eolic\' power is another word for wind power.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7685-949b-af2c3b823739","description":"Wind","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7737-b1cb-57d807e0d7a1","description":"Solar","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad4f-7653-8d65-886146730e59","de